  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quilombola women&apos;s protagonism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quilombola communities in the Brazilian state of Minas Gerais that have historically lived off their land are now struggling and being displaced by drought and other environmental challenges. The IAF supports community-led solutions for producers to expand their economic opportunities, leadership skills, and financial autonomy in Brazil. IAF grantee Federa??o das Comunidades Quilombolas de Minas Gerais (N?Golo) is working with Quilombola women in Minas Gerais to develop sustainable practices in sustainable agriculture and promote gender equity. The grant will bolster their social and economic autonomy by improving productive practices, strengthening their existing Quilombola associations, and providing training in cooperative development, social entrepreneurship, and women?s leadership. This grant is part of the IAF?s Women INvesting in Growth and Security (WINGS) initiative to empower women as business and community leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
